insert into pages (urlpath, content) values
    (
        '(header)',
        E'<nav class=\"header bar\">\n  <ul>\n    <li><a class=\"nav\" href=\"/calendars/events/\">Full Schedule</a></li>\n    <li><a class=\"nav\" href=\"/login\">Artist Login</a></li>\n    <li><a class=\"nav\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd2lZxTndl2riVHEyBuEVNcC8Q9u8s44oCvwSdLo6w7Bqx74w/viewform?usp=header\">Volunteer</a></li>\n  </ul>\n</nav>'
    ),
    (
        '(footer)',
        E'<div class=\"footer flex flex-row justify-around mt2 mb1\">\n  <a href=\"/\">Home</a>\n  <a href=\"/about/\">About</a>\n  <a href=\"/contact/\">Contact</a>\n  <a href=\"/cur-events/\">Current Events</a>\n</div>\n'
    ),
    (
        '(site-name)',
        'Allentown ReFringe'
    ),
    (
        '(opengraph)',
        E'    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Allentown ReFringe\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Collaborative Arts Showcase\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"ReFringe.org\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://refringe.mandelics.com\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://refringe.mandelics.com/img/refringe-ogp2.jpg\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"ReFringe Flyer\" />\n'
    ),
    (
        '/',
        E'# Allentown ReFringe\n\n**The Allentown ReFringe is designed as a collaborative arts showcase, scheduled for May 14-17, 2026. We will attempt to fill Allentown with experimental works that blend community and creativity. We hope to feature unusual art in unusual spaces. Artists from all disciplines–and those who mix them–are encouraged to collaborate.**\n\n<video controls loop autoplay loading=\"lazy\"><source src=\"/img/refringe.mp4\"></video>\n'
    ),
    (
        '/about/',
        E'# About\n\n## The Allentown ReFringe 2026\n\n#### **May 14 - 17, 2026**\n\n#### ReFringe Allentown: Year Zero\n\nAllentown, rich in history and creativity, is ready for renewal. The Allentown ReFringe embraces this moment, aware that we are the stewards of what’s next. A grassroots festival should reflect and benefit its people, so we keep ReFringe walkable within our vibrant community. When artists and audiences explore together, we create shared experiences that connect spaces and people. By localizing resources, we maximize impact. Allentown offers everything nearby—venues, parks, creative spaces—turning our community into a canvas, closing the gap between artist and audience weaving the festival into the neighborhood’s fabric. We’re ready for rediscovery, seeking to fill a void felt by those who wish to create and share something that belongs to us all.\n\n#### What ReFringe Offers\n\nThis is a different kind of festival, which celebrates what we can achieve together. We welcome all artists, but initial constraints may place a practical limit on full bands, in adhering to our principles of transforming spaces without compromise. We hope venues will join in as needed resources, seeing what we can do with what we have. We’re not rejecting traditional acts; we’re focusing on our shared resources and the diverse creativity we aim to cultivate, offering unique environments otherwise unavailable. We ask artists to be flexible and open to new collaborations. Your adaptability enriches our ability to craft a unique experience.\n\n#### Microsponsorship and Community Support\n\nWe keep events free for all, instead advocating a culture of microsponsorship—directly supporting artists for the value of the experience, however intangible. This keeps the festival accessible while helping artists sustain their craft. We aim to make this kind of direct support a cultural norm, reaching those unaware of its potential impact. By encouraging attendees to document and share their stories as well, we preserve the experience and make everyone integral to our collective effort and leave a roadmap for future efforts.\n\n#### Why We Do This Together\n\nReFringe is about building a chorus, where every contribution matters. We’re creating systems that work for us—valuing artists, benefiting the community, and giving everyone a voice. Designed by its very stakeholders, ReFringe is a collaboration among artists, organizers, and the neighborhood, demonstrating that we’re building the future one step at a time whenever we can work together.\n\n#### The Promise of Year Zero\n\nYear Zero marks our beginning. This is about reclaiming potential in spaces and in ourselves. There’s no telling what we can achieve. The Allentown ReFringe offers a space to build together. It’s a model of what happens when creativity, collaboration, and community intersect, using our streets and resources to create something that extends beyond this moment. We begin by simply coming together. If it works, it’s because we believed in it and in each other. With this mutual shared permission we can reactivate this creative potential, this neighborhood, this movement.\n\n**Let’s make it up as we go along—together.**\n**May 14th-17th, 2026**\n**Everywhere, Allentown, Buffalo, NY**\n**>>STAY TUNED>> www.refringe.org **\n'
    ),
    (
        '/contact/',
        E'# Contact\n\n**Questions? Please email us.**\n\nInformation about ReFringe: info@refringe.org\n\nWebsite Concerns: webmaster@refringe.org\n'
    ),
    (
        '/cur-events/',
        E'# Current Events\n\n'
    );
